<header class="site-header"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Programming the Loop home"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt=""/>Programming the Loop</a><nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/learn/">Learn</a><a href="/experiments/">Experiments</a><a href="/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a class="nav-ebook" href="/downloads/">Free ebook ↗</a></nav><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mobile-menu">Menu</button><nav class="mobile-panel" id="mobile-menu" aria-label="Mobile navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/learn/">Learn</a><a href="/experiments/">Experiments</a><a href="/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/downloads/">Free ebook ↗</a></nav></div></header>
<main><section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Independent engineering research · First edition / October 2026</div><h1>Programming<br/>the <span>Loop</span></h1><p class="lede"><strong>Better coding agents start with better engineering.</strong> Learn what makes coding agents effective, what makes them fail, and which practices actually justify their cost.</p><p class="fineprint">Evidence-led guidance drawn from practical experiments, reproducible code and real measurements.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/learn/">Start learning <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button" href="/experiments/">Explore experiments</a></div><p class="fineprint">Also available: <a class="text-link" href="/downloads/">download the free ebook ↗</a></p></div>
<div class="loop-card" aria-label="Coding-agent feedback loop diagram"><div class="loop-top"><span>Execution loop / 001</span><span>Feedback enabled</span></div><svg class="loop-svg" viewBox="0 0 540 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="loop-title loop-desc"><title id="loop-title">A coding agent feedback loop</title><desc id="loop-desc">Task, agent, code, and verification form a loop. Feedback flows from verification back to the agent.</desc><defs><marker id="arrow" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L7 3.5 0 7" fill="none" stroke="#55e6d0" stroke-width="1.3"/></marker></defs><path class="loop-path" marker-end="url(#arrow)" d="M142 76H370M427 96V210M370 240H142M112 210V100"/><path d="M260 241v52H93V100" fill="none" stroke="#9b8cff" stroke-dasharray="3 7" stroke-width="1.4" opacity=".8" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/><rect class="loop-node" x="35" y="48" rx="9" width="140" height="56"/><rect class="loop-node active" x="360" y="48" rx="9" width="140" height="56"/><rect class="loop-node" x="360" y="210" rx="9" width="140" height="56"/><rect class="loop-node" x="35" y="210" rx="9" width="140" height="56"/><text class="loop-label" x="105" y="81" text-anchor="middle">01 / TASK</text><text class="loop-label" x="430" y="81" text-anchor="middle">02 / AGENT</text><text class="loop-label" x="430" y="243" text-anchor="middle">03 / CODE</text><text class="loop-label" x="105" y="243" text-anchor="middle">04 / VERIFY</text><text x="265" y="309" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9b8cff" font-family="DM Mono,monospace" font-size="10">OBSERVED FEEDBACK → AGENT</text><circle cx="260" cy="159" r="42" fill="#101b2b" stroke="#29364a"/><circle cx="260" cy="159" r="24" fill="none" stroke="#55e6d0" stroke-width="1.3"/><path d="M251 159a9 9 0 1 1 9 9" fill="none" stroke="#55e6d0" stroke-width="2"/><path d="m258 166 3 3 4-4" fill="none" stroke="#55e6d0" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="260" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ba9bf" font-family="DM Mono,monospace" font-size="9">CHECK · LEARN · REPEAT</text></svg><div class="loop-foot"><span class="signal"></span> Verification turns output into usable feedback</div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Evidence, with the limits attached</div><h2>What the trials found</h2></div><p>Small controlled studies. Useful signals, not universal laws. Every result sits beside the conditions that produced it.</p></div><div class="findings"><article class="finding"><span class="label">Measured finding · Experiment J</span><div class="number">+35–48%</div><h3>More tokens, no reliable correctness gain</h3><p>A fully agent-optimised Java repository used more tokens. Correctness and structure-question differences were within noise in the tested tasks.</p><p class="limitation">One repository and model; mechanical edits and structure questions; 8 runs per task per arm. Four repository ingredients were tested together.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learn/right-facts/">Read the analysis →</a></article><article class="finding"><span class="label">Measured finding · Cross-repository</span><div class="number">3 → 18–19 / 20</div><h3>Missing dependency facts changed the result</h3><p>Storefront runs passed hidden tests far more often when given relevant backend knowledge; a small note or API contract later performed about as well.</p><p class="limitation">Five runs per task, identifiers renamed by the author, one model. This is a case study, not a general success rate.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learn/right-facts/">Read the analysis →</a></article><article class="finding"><span class="label">Measured finding · Verification</span><div class="number">12 / 12</div><h3>Self-reported checks can miss a broken proof</h3><p>All runs reported a passing check while the brief’s real-service criterion remained unverified. In the no-contract arm, agents changed the freshness gate.</p><p class="limitation">One model, one task, 6 runs per arm. With the real contract, all 6 runs were correct.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learn/proof-not-promises/">Read the analysis →</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose a path</div><h2>Learn the engineering around the agent</h2></div><p>Move from task design to evidence, then build a workflow that earns trust through verification.</p></div><div class="paths"><a class="path-card" href="/learn/agent-foundations/"><span class="path-num">01 — FOUNDATION</span><h3>Agent Foundations</h3><p>Understand agent loops and design tasks that can be completed and checked.</p></a><a class="path-card" href="/learn/right-facts/"><span class="path-num">02 — CONTEXT</span><h3>Context and Knowledge</h3><p>Learn when documentation, contracts, skills and code graphs help or hinder.</p></a><a class="path-card" href="/learn/proof-not-promises/"><span class="path-num">03 — VERIFICATION</span><h3>Verification and Harness</h3><p>Build trustworthy checks and useful feedback into coding workflows.</p></a><a class="path-card" href="/learn/parallel-agents/"><span class="path-num">04 — SCALE</span><h3>Scaling and Measuring</h3><p>Explore parallel agents, engineering reviews, cost and reproducible experiments.</p></a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Research log</div><h2>Experiments, in the open</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/experiments/">View research index →</a></div><div class="experiment-list"><a class="experiment-card" href="/learn/right-facts/"><span class="status">Published</span><div><h3>Repository guidance and token cost</h3><p>Experiment J · Results and limitations from the first edition.</p></div></a><a class="experiment-card" href="/experiments/knowing-when-you-dont-know/"><span class="status planned">Planned</span><div><h3>Knowing When You Don’t Know</h3><p>Can signposting help agents find authoritative external dependencies?</p></div></a></div></div></section>
